omit-content-attribution-from-wire-requests

Lane: bugfix

FlatPatch: omit-content-attribution-from-wire-requests

Form: GitDiff

Segment: none

Purpose: Prevent Responses and Responses Lite schema rejection of unsupported per-content attribution.

Requires: none

Provides: Remove content_item_metadata only from the formatted wire-request copy for HTTP and WebSocket Responses while retaining supported metadata and local prompt provenance.

Boundary: Preserve content-item classifications, turn metadata, content, local history and compaction attribution, model selection, transport and retry behavior; do not import an upstream fix.

Verification: Responses Lite and standard request tests assert attribution absence on initial and resumed inputs while preserving instructions, content classifications, tools and stable retained prefixes; native provenance tests retain local attribution.


